  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.5.0.0\n\t\t\t- Breaking for every host that implements the storage port: ISecurityAudit has a new Operation property (string, optional), what was accessed: an endpoint as its method and route, such as \"POST api/STU3/Patient/$getstructuredrecord\", or a fully qualified operation or namespace name. Your SecurityAudit entity must implement it, and your database needs a new column for it and a migration: nullable, up to 500 characters (nvarchar(500) on SQL Server). Existing rows keep NULL.\n\t\t\t- SecurityAuditClient.LogSecurityAuditAsync and RecordSecurityAuditAsync, the versions that take values, have a new optional operation parameter after tokenId and before the CancellationToken. It is copied onto the entry as given. A call that passes the token by position straight after tokenId no longer compiles: name it (cancellationToken: cancellationToken) or pass the operation before it. Recompile anything that calls these methods, and update mock set-ups and verifications of them.\n\t\t\t- Operation is free text, up to 500 characters: the host chooses its convention and keeps to it, and the library neither parses nor interprets it. It must never hold a query string, an NHS number or any other patient identifier; for an endpoint, record its route template, not the path a request was sent to.\n\t\t\t- A security audit whose Operation is longer than 500 characters is refused on add and modify. Null is allowed.\n\t\t\t- Audits and metrics are unchanged.\n\t\t\t- Upgrade guide: https://github.com/NHSISL/NHSOneLondon.AuditAndMetrics#upgrading-from-04x",
